  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "Characterized as \"the perfect soundtrack to limb-threatening aerial stunts\" and \"thrash metal’s snotty younger brother,\" skate punk is also known as \"skate rock\" and \"skatecore\". Noted by AllMusic for having \"high-energy\", skate punk features fast tempos. Many of the original skate punk bands in the 1980s were hardcore punk bands. In the 1990s, this changed when more bands began to play a style of skate punk that sounded more like pop punk and standard punk rock than hardcore punk. Also a skater subculture, skate punk's origins go back to skate culture and surf culture. Author Sharon M."
